      "content": "Thanks for the pointers. Regarding point A, if I'm going to properly debunk the rhetoric, I need to understand how they actually constructed those arguments. In the 1950s, how did they use \"science\" or social theories to claim that segregation actually prevented social friction or maintain \"social stability\"? I want to see how they framed the idea that integrating different groups would lead to \"chaos\" or \"decline\"—like, what was the specific logic they used to argue that keeping the races separate was actually the more \"orderly\" or \"rational\" choice for the community at that time?",
